# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# VisionWorx 360 Estimator — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local, fill in your keys, then restart
# the dev server. In production, set these in Vercel →
# Settings → Environment Variables.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── AI: Estimate generation + Voice transcription ─────────────────
# Recommended. Enables GPT-4o (vision + estimates) AND Whisper voice.
# Get key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...

# Alternative / fallback: Claude for estimate generation only.
# Not needed if you have OPENAI_API_KEY.
# Get key: https://console.anthropic.com
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Priority: OPENAI_API_KEY → ANTHROPIC_API_KEY → Demo mode

# ── Live Material Prices (Home Depot / Lowe's) ────────────────────
# Option A: BigBox API (recommended) — Home Depot product search
# ~$50/month for 5,000 searches. Free tier available.
# Get key: https://bigboxapi.com
BIGBOX_API_KEY=

# Option B: SerpAPI — alternative Home Depot data source
# ~$50/month. Use if you don't have BigBox.
# Get key: https://serpapi.com
SERPAPI_KEY=

# Without either key, the app uses built-in regional price simulation.
# Priority: BIGBOX_API_KEY → SERPAPI_KEY → simulated prices

# ── Labor Rates ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No external API needed — labor rates are calculated from the
# BLS OES 2023 database built into the app (lib/labor-rates.ts).
# No key required.

# ── Supabase (optional — sync data across devices) ───────────────
# Connect to Supabase to store estimates, profiles, and customers
# in a real database instead of browser localStorage.
# Get these from: Supabase Dashboard → Project → Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# After adding Supabase keys, run the schema migration:
#   npx supabase db push
# or apply supabase/migrations/001_initial.sql manually in the
# Supabase SQL Editor.
